    "description": "AI-search visibility (Generative Engine Optimization, or GEO) is how often and how favorably ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Claude mention your brand when they answer queries in your space.",
    "html": "<h2>What AI-search visibility actually measures</h2>\n<p><strong>AI-search visibility</strong> — often called Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) — is the share of times a leading LLM (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude) names your brand when it answers a query in your category. Classic SEO asks \"what position are we in the search results?\" GEO asks a different question: \"when a buyer asks an AI for a recommendation, does it mention us?\"</p>\n<p>A citation is not the same as a backlink. The model may describe your product in prose, compare you to a competitor, or list you as an option — all without a clickable link. What you want to track is whether the model <em>surfaced</em> you at all, and in what light.</p>\n<h2>Why it matters now</h2>\n<p>Buyers are increasingly skipping the blue links. They open ChatGPT or Perplexity and ask \"what's the best tool for X?\" or \"how should I do Y?\" If the answer names a competitor and not you, you lose the first touch — before a search result page is ever seen.</p>\n<p>This is not a future problem. LLM answers already shape consideration in software, finance, and how-to categories. Teams that measure it can act on it; teams that don't are flying blind on a channel that is already live.</p>\n<h2>What gets measured</h2>\n<p>A useful GEO signal has three parts:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Citation rate per query</strong> — of the runs where the engine answered your query, how many named your brand?</li><li><strong>Citation rate per engine</strong> — ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Claude do not agree; one may cite you while another ignores you.</li><li><strong>Competitor gap</strong> — on each query, who else got named instead of (or alongside) you?</li></ul>\n<p>Together these give a directional trend: are you gaining or losing share of voice inside AI answers, and where exactly.</p>\n<h2>What it cannot do</h2>\n<p>A visibility tracker shows you the current state and the gaps. It does <strong>not</strong> control what the model decides to cite, and it cannot guarantee a citation. LLM answers also vary between runs and accounts, so counts are sampled trends, not audit-grade statistics.</p>\n<p>Treat GEO tracking as a dashboard, not a lever. The lever is still your content, authority, and how clearly you answer each query.</p>\n<h2>Authoritative references</h2>\n<ul><li>Google Search Central (how search and AI Overviews treat content): https://developers.google.com/search/docs</li><li>OpenAI (how ChatGPT answers are produced): https://openai.com/blog</li></ul>\n",
